 Experiment 50: To Perform Smoke and Load Testing on a Newly Deployed Government Service Website to Verify Availability and Performance of Critical Pages

AIM
To perform smoke testing and load testing on a newly deployed government service website using Apache JMeter to verify the availability and performance of critical pages.

ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter.
2. Create a new Test Plan.
3. Add a Thread Group to the Test Plan.
4. Configure one user for smoke testing.
5. Add HTTP Request Samplers for critical website pages.
6. Enter the government website URL and select the GET method.
7. Add Response Assertions to verify successful HTTP status codes.
8. Run the smoke test and check page availability.
9. Increase the number of users to 100 for load testing.
10. Configure the ramp-up period and loop count.
11. Run the load test and collect performance results.
12. Analyze response time, throughput, and error rate.

CONFIGURATION

| Parameter | Smoke Testing | Load Testing |
|---|---|---|
| Testing Tool | Apache JMeter | Apache JMeter |
| Number of Users | 1 | 100 |
| Ramp-up Period | 1 second | 50 seconds |
| Loop Count | 1 | 1 |
| Request Method | GET | GET |
| Test Type | Availability | Performance |

## INPUT

**Sample website URL:**

```text
https://example.gov.in
```

**Critical pages to test:**
1. Home Page
2. Login Page
3. Registration Page
4. Service Information Page

**Request Method:** GET

**Expected HTTP Status Code:** 200 OK

